{"message":"The savings selection does not have to come first. However, opening the replacement checking account before closing Light Blue is safer: you avoid a gap in checking access, and you retain an active checking relationship for the savings-account eligibility requirement. If you close Light Blue first, you can still open the replacement checking account, but you may need to wait until the new checking account has been open for 14 days before opening savings.

For early direct deposit, Bluest’s documented benefits do not specify early paycheck access. Evergreen does: eligible paychecks may arrive up to 2 days early. Evergreen also earns 0.05% APY and provides a 0.15% boost when paired with Diamond Elite savings, or a 0.55% boost when paired with Green savings.

I recommend opening an Evergreen Account first, then closing the Light Blue Account once the new account is confirmed. Please confirm that you want the Evergreen Account as your replacement checking account. If you still want Light Blue closed first, say so explicitly; I’ll first check the closure requirements, including pending transactions."}
